problems.problem:
Find all functions $f$ from the integers to the integers satisfying
(i) $f(n)f(-n) = f(n^2)$;
(ii) $f(m+n) = f(m) + f(n) + 2mn$.

Find all monic polynomials $P$ satisfying the following conditions:
(i) $P(x + P(x)) = x^2 + P(P(x))$ for every real value $x$;
(ii) $P(0) < -1$.

A contest has a certain number of contestants and a certain number of judges. Each of the judges makes a full classification of the contestants. The judges get together and produce the official ranking of the contestants. For each pair of contestants $A$ and $B$, if $A$ was ranked higher than $B$ in the official classification, then the number of judges who agree with it is strictly larger than the number of judges who disagree. It is known that all the judges' rankings are different and they are all different from the official ranking. Determine the maximum possible number of judges if
(a) there are 4 contestants;
(b) there are $n$ contestants.

There are 3000 lamps numbered from 0 to 2999 on a circle, and each of them has three possible states: off, medium light and full light. If a lamp in the off state is activated, it changes to medium light; if it is in medium light, it changes to full light; and if it is in full light, it turns off. In front of each lamp there is a switch which activates the corresponding lamp twice and activates each of the two adjacent lamps once. Assuming that all lamps are off at the beginning, determine whether it is possible to reach the following arrangements of the lamps:
(a) lamp 0 is in full light and all the others are off;
(b) the lamps of the form $6k$ and $6k+1$ are in full light and the rest of them are off.
